<title>BRAZIL: Brazil soybean crop 90 pct harvested - Safras.</title>
<headline>Brazil soybean crop 90 pct harvested - Safras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Around 90 percent of Brazil's expected soybean crop had been harvested by April 24, consultants Safras e Mercado said in a weekly report.</p>
<p>The 90 percent compares with 78 percent by April 25, 1996, and a historical average over the past five years of 72 percent, it added.</p>
<p>A breakdown of percentage harvested by state follows.</p>
<p> STATE		     25/04/97   17/04/97  25/04/96 5-yr avge</p>
<p> Rio Grande do Sul	 86	    64	   60	  56</p>
<p> Parana			98	    94	   91	  92</p>
<p> Mato Grosso		 95	    90	   90	  83</p>
<p> Mato Grosso do Sul	96	    92	   91	  84</p>
<p> Goias			 90	    83	   90	  63</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		  100	   100	  100	  96</p>
<p> Minas Gerais		62	    55	   57	  49</p>
<p> Others			74	    50	   57	  53</p>
<p> TOTAL BRAZIL		90	    80	   78	  72</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
</text>
